       On success, these functions return the number of input  items  success‐
       fully  matched  and  assigned;  this can be fewer than provided for, or
       even zero, in the event of an early matching failure.

       The value EEOOFF is returned if the end of input is reached before  either
       the  first  successful conversion or a matching failure occurs.  EEOOFF is
       also returned if a read error occurs, in which case the error indicator
       for the stream (see ffeerrrroorr(3)) is set, and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
       error.

